module gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.verification_bound_to_the_revision_it_started_on

import std.types { NonEmptyStr }
import gunbc.recurring_failure_mode { RecurringFailureMode }

data verification_bound_to_the_revision_it_started_on: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "verification_bound_to_the_revision_it_started_on" as NonEmptyStr,

  receipts: [
    "**a verification attributed to the revision it STARTED on rather than the one it FINISHED against** (a checkout is a fact about an INSTANT; a build, a regeneration or a test run consumes an INTERVAL. If the working tree changes anywhere inside that interval -- a branch switch, a merge, a colleague's push into a shared worktree, an editor save -- the artifact that gets exercised is the tree as of the READ, and the revision the author names is the tree as of the LAUNCH. The result is real and the subject is wrong. ",

    "WHAT MAKES IT INVISIBLE IS THAT EVERY INTERMEDIATE SIGNAL IS CORRECT. The compile really compiled, the evaluation really returned, the exit code is really zero; nothing in the transcript is false, and nothing in it names a revision either. The only false proposition is the one the author supplies afterwards from memory, which is why it survives careful reading of the log -- the log does not contain the claim being checked. ",

    "IT IS WORST WHERE THE TWO TREES ARE NEARLY IDENTICAL, because then the result reproduces and the misattribution is never caught, so the HABIT is ratified rather than the reasoning. The occasion it does not reproduce is the occasion where the tree difference mattered, i.e. exactly the case the verification was supposed to decide. ",

    "RECOGNITION RULE: ASK WHICH REVISION WAS CHECKED OUT WHEN THE RUN FINISHED, NOT WHEN IT STARTED, and demand the answer as an immutable identifier rather than a branch name -- a branch name is itself a mutable binding, so 'I ran it on the control branch' is the same failure one level up. A local verification is bankable only as RESULT + EXACT IMMUTABLE SUBJECT REVISION + ACQUISITION TIME; a result missing any of the three names an unidentified subject. ",

    "SPECIMEN, gunbc#10327. The positive-control witness for the preemption-reachability column was compiled and evaluated locally and reported as verified before push. The build had been launched from the control branch but FINISHED after a switch to `session/vivid-ibex-751-cost-receipts`, whose source-root is a strict SUPERSET of the shipped one -- three additional `recurring_failure_mode` rows and their roster imports. The witness file was untracked and byte-identical across both trees so the result is very probably reproducible, but 'very probably reproducible' is a PREDICTION about the shipped tree and had been written down as a RECEIPT for it. Corrected in the PR body by naming the head that actually ran and naming CI's floor run as the first execution against the shipped tree. ",

    "IT IS NOT `window_rendered_subject_misattribution` AND MERGING THEM LOSES THE REMEDY. There, a correctly measured figure is attributed to the wrong subject because a rendering window cropped the subject; the defect is in the READ and a wider read fixes it. Here the measurement is attributed to the wrong revision of the RIGHT subject, the defect is in the WRITE, and no amount of re-reading the output recovers the revision -- the information was never captured. It is also distinct from `absent_artifact_may_be_measuring_instrument_vintage`: there the INSTRUMENT is stale against a current subject; here the instrument is current and the SUBJECT is not the one claimed. ",

    "RUNG FOUND AT: MITIGATABLE. The harm is contained only by the author noticing and restating the revision, which is a discipline and not a mechanism, and the containing act happens after the false sentence has already been circulated. ",

    "ATTAINABLE CEILING: STRUCTURALLY GUARANTEED, and not higher, because the invalid state remains describable -- a human can always type a revision into prose. Membership is nonetheless decidable by the runner itself: the tree identity is readable at the moment of the READ, so a verification receipt that CARRIES the revision it observed, rather than accepting one asserted alongside it, cannot name a tree it did not exercise. What no in-repository construction can prevent is an author transcribing a receipt into a sentence, which is the same residue DESIGN's name-the-instrument rule already addresses. ",

    "NEXT-RUNG TRIGGER: A VERIFICATION RECEIPT CARRIER WHOSE SUBJECT REVISION IS READ BY THE RUNNER AT COMPLETION AND WHICH REFUSES WHEN THE TREE MOVED MID-RUN -- sufficient for a local run that spans a branch switch to be a REFUSAL rather than a result with an author-supplied revision. A trigger naming only 'record the sha' is the artifact-grained version of this and is satisfied by recording the sha at launch, which is precisely the value that is wrong. ",

    "**AN AUTOMATED VERIFIER EXHIBITS THIS CLASS TOO, AND THE TWO PRODUCERS DIFFER IN WHICH WALL IS EVEN AVAILABLE TO THEM (2026-09-08, gunbc#10840).** The row above is written around a human author naming a revision from memory. THE SAME INVALID STATE ARRIVES FROM A MACHINE THAT NEVER CONSULTS ITS MEMORY AT ALL: a code review is an INTERVAL -- read the diff, reason, submit -- and a reviewer that resolves the head when it STARTS stamps a verdict about a commit that may no longer be the head when it FINISHES. MEASURED: commit 91a78035ed at 16:03:18Z, commit 688b08dcf6 at 17:16:44Z, and GitHub review 5144886543 SUBMITTED AT 17:19:16Z -- two and a half minutes after the newer head existed -- carrying commit_id 91a78035ed. Its own text discusses a field named `reconsider_when`, which exists ONLY in 688b08dcf6, so THE REVIEWER READ THE NEWER TREE AND STAMPED THE OLDER REVISION. Result real, subject wrong, every intermediate signal correct. ",

    "**THE NEAR-MISS IS STATED AS A NEAR-MISS RATHER THAN INFLATED, because this row's own analysis predicts exactly this shape.** The verdict was RIGHT ABOUT THE CODE and wrong only about the label -- the content it examined is the content on the current head -- which is the arm above that says the class is worst where the two trees are nearly identical, since the result reproduces and the habit is ratified. THE HARM THAT DID OCCUR IS DOWNSTREAM AND SMALL AND IS RECORDED AT ITS REAL SIZE: a reviewer of the review could not tell a content-current verdict from a genuinely stale one, so the approval was declined as on-head authority and a re-review was spent that the content did not require. A row claiming more than that here would be the inflation this ledger exists to catch. ",

    "**THE TRANSFERABLE HALF IS THAT THE GUARD DOES NOT TRANSFER.** Two review producers act on this repository and BOTH are subject to this class, but the wall available to each is different in kind. THE API-REVIEWER HOLDS A WORKTREE, so it can compare two trees, and it already does: its `prepareWorktree` freshness check refused a run outright with `worktree freshness check failed: HEAD is <a> but PR head is <b> -- refusing to review a stale/wrong checkout`, which is this class caught at the wall and is why that producer contributes no specimen here. THAT REFUSAL IS OBSERVED TWICE UNDER TWO DIFFERENT PROVIDERS, WHICH IS WHAT MAKES THE PARTITION TWO PRODUCERS RATHER THAN THREE: on gunbc#10832 the same guard fired for a `claude` run and for a `cursor` run -- review 62538 and review 62438 -- with the identical message and the identical frame through `prepareWorktree` in the api-reviewer's own script. So `claude` and `cursor` are PROVIDERS INSIDE ONE PRODUCER, not independent instruments that happen to agree, and the partition rests on the property named here -- holds a worktree versus reads an API -- rather than on any provider name, which is also why it survives either being renamed. BOUNDED HONESTLY: both observed refusals are the SAME DIRECTION, a checkout NEWER than the recorded pull-request head, verified by ancestry rather than by reading the message. The guard is therefore demonstrated in one direction only, and whether it refuses a checkout that is BEHIND the head is untested here and is not claimed. THE SIDE-CHAT REVIEWER HAS NO CHECKOUT AT ALL -- it reads the pull request through the API and names whatever revision it decided on -- so a checkout comparison is not merely absent there, it is UNAVAILABLE, and citing the api-reviewer's guard as the fix would name a mechanism that producer cannot host. ITS GUARD IS A DIFFERENT ONE: re-read the pull request head immediately before submitting, stamp THAT, and refuse to submit when the head moved while it was reasoning. ",

    "SO THE OBLIGATION TRANSFERS AND THE IMPLEMENTATION DOES NOT, which is the correction worth carrying past this specimen: `the other producer already solved it` is true here and is not a repair, because one instrument compares two TREES and the other can only compare two reads of one API. NEXT-RUNG TRIGGER FOR THE REVIEW-PRODUCER POPULATION, at capability grain: EVERY REVIEW PRODUCER RESOLVES ITS SUBJECT REVISION AT SUBMIT AND REFUSES WHEN THAT REVISION IS NOT THE ONE IT EXAMINED -- sufficient for a verdict submitted after its subject moved to be a refusal rather than a verdict wearing the previous head's identity. A trigger naming a checkout comparison would be satisfiable by only one of the two producers and dead for the other, which is the same artifact-versus-capability defect this row's own trigger paragraph warns about one line above.)",
  ],

  evidence: [],
}
